facts:
At a zero of **multiplicity 1**, the curve **cuts** straight through the $x$-axis.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-2.2,0) -- (3.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-2.8) -- (0,2.8) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-1.2:3.2,smooth,variable=\x,samples=60] plot ({\x},{0.9*(\x-1)+0.05*(\x-1)*(\x-1)*(\x-1)});
\filldraw (1,0) circle (2pt) node[below right] {$\alpha$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

At a zero of **even multiplicity** ($m = 2, 4, \ldots$), the curve **touches** the $x$-axis and turns back without crossing.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-2.2,0) -- (3.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-0.9) -- (0,3.1) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-1.2:3.2,smooth,variable=\x,samples=60] plot ({\x},{0.55*(\x-1)*(\x-1)});
\filldraw (1,0) circle (2pt) node[below] {$\alpha$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

At a zero of **odd multiplicity $\ge 3$** ($m = 3, 5, \ldots$), the curve **flattens** along the $x$-axis as it crosses.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-2.2,0) -- (3.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-2.7) -- (0,2.7) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-1.2:3.2,smooth,variable=\x,samples=60] plot ({\x},{0.22*(\x-1)*(\x-1)*(\x-1)});
\filldraw (1,0) circle (2pt) node[below] {$\alpha$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.question_text:
For the polynomial graphed below, identify the zeroes and state whether each has odd or even multiplicity:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-4,0) -- (4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-3) -- (0,3) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-2.6:3.5,smooth,variable=\x,samples=60] plot ({\x},{0.15*(\x+2)*(\x-3)*(\x-3)});
\filldraw (-2,0) circle (2pt) node[below left] {$-2$};
\filldraw (3,0) circle (2pt) node[below] {$3$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.question_text:
Identify the zero that has multiplicity $3$ on the graph below and explain how the visual feature confirms it:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-4,0) -- (3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-3) -- (0,3) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-3.2:1.35,smooth,variable=\x,samples=60] plot ({\x},{0.2*(\x+2)*(\x+2)*(\x+2)*(1-\x)});
\filldraw (-2,0) circle (2pt) node[below] {$-2$};
\filldraw (1,0) circle (2pt) node[below] {$1$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

mastery.question_text:
The monic quartic polynomial shown below touches the $x$-axis at $x = -2$ and $x = 3$.
Find its equation and evaluate its $y$-intercept.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-4,0) -- (5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-1) -- (0,4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-2.7:3.7,smooth,variable=\x,samples=60] plot ({\x},{0.1*(\x+2)*(\x+2)*(\x-3)*(\x-3)});
\filldraw (-2,0) circle (2pt) node[below] {$-2$};
\filldraw (3,0) circle (2pt) node[below] {$3$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
